    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change lives entirely in one small function class, `AssignCustomerCode.java`:\n\n- **New format** `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`: the `service` method now builds the code from both a city prefix and a last-name prefix, with a per-city sequence.\n- **Per-city sequence**: `citySequence` counts existing owners whose city matches (case-insensitively) and adds one, instead of the old global owner count.\n- **Shared `prefix` helper**: the \"upper-cased first three letters\" logic is factored into a tiny static method reused for both city and last name.\n\n**Why nothing else needed touching:** the membership number in `OwnerMapper` is derived at mapping time via `owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + ...`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format \u2014 no edit required. Everything built from the customer code flows from that single source.\n\n**Structural impact:** one file touched, one existing method changed. The two new helpers are small, cohesive, private static methods with near-zero surrounding complexity \u2014 behaviour was added as new units rather than by growing the existing method or class.",
